{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 26,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How hast thou helped him that is without power!\nHow hast thou saved the arm that hath no strength!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How hast thou counselled him that hath no wisdom,\nAnd plentifully declared sound knowledge!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom hast thou uttered words?\nAnd whose spirit came forth from thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that are deceased tremble\nBeneath the waters and the inhabitants thereof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sheol is naked before ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",\nAnd Abaddon hath no covering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He stretcheth out the north over empty space,\nAnd hangeth the earth upon nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He bindeth up the waters in his thick clouds;\nAnd the cloud is not rent under them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He incloseth the face of his throne,\nAnd spreadeth his cloud upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath described a boundary upon the face of the waters,\nUnto the confines of light and darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The pillars of heaven tremble\nAnd are astonished at his rebuke.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He stirreth up the sea with his power,\nAnd by his understanding he smiteth through Rahab.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By his Spirit the heavens are garnished;\nHis hand hath pierced the swift serpent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.26.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.26.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, these are but the outskirts of his ways:\nAnd how small a whisper do we hear of him!\nBut the thunder of his power who can understand?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
